# XDG_config

Personal dotfiles repo synced between laptop and PC via git (+ sshfs/git-sync-tui).

## Machines

- **This PC** — Linux Mint + i3 + X11 + polybar (see `linux-mint-i3` rule)
- **Laptop** — Hyprland + Waybar (remote via `sshfs/connect-laptop.sh`)

## Layout

- `i3/`, `polybar/`, `picom/`, `rofi/`, `nvim/`, `alacritty/` — symlinked into `~/.config/` via `attach.sh` (this PC)
- `hypr/`, `waybar/` — laptop (Hyprland); also linked by `attach.sh` but not the local runtime target
- `sshfs/` — laptop mount (`connect-laptop.sh`) and `git-sync-tui` for cross-machine repo sync
- `sshfs/git-sync-tui/` — Rust TUI: git push/pull + Cursor chat sync via cursaves

## Cross-machine workflow

- Code: git remotes per project; use `git-sync-tui` when comparing local vs `/mnt/remote/...`
- Cursor chats: synced with `cursaves` (private `~/.cursaves` git remote), not project git
- Quit Cursor before importing chats on the other machine; restart Cursor after import

## Editing

- Keep changes minimal and match existing style in each config subtree
- Do not commit secrets, tokens, or machine-specific paths unless already present as examples
